        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
      <item row="2" column="1">
       <widget class="QPushButton" name="captureButton">
        <property name="enabled">
         <bool>false</bool>
        </property>
        <property name="toolTip">
         <string>Freeze LiveView, save the frame, run UC1 and the blood-vessel enhancement (UC2) in the background on the recorded calibrated cube, and show the cube in HS Cube. The acquisition is simulated. Available while the camera runs and no capture is in progress.</string>
        </property>
        <property name="text">
         <string>Capture</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
      <item row="3" column="0">
       <widget class="QLabel" name="resultOutputLabel">
        <property name="text">
         <string>Delineation output:</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
      <item row="3" column="1">
       <widget class="QComboBox" name="resultOutputSelector">
        <property name="enabled">
         <bool>false</bool>
        </property>
        <property name="toolTip">
         <string>Select what the Tumour Delineation panel shows. Each UC1 output is shown on its own, as UC1 wrote it. gtMap is the recorded case&apos;s own labelling from the HSI Human Brain Database, drawn over the output chosen last: green normal tissue, red tumour, blue hypervascularised, black background, unlabelled pixels left clear. svm.bmp and knn.bmp use those same colours, so they can be read against it directly.</string>
        </property>
        <property name="SlicerParameterName" stdset="0">
         <string>resultOutput</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
      <item row="4" column="0">
       <widget class="QLabel" name="cubeDisplayLabel">
        <property name="text">
         <string>HS Cube shows:</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
      <item row="4" column="1">
       <widget class="QComboBox" name="cubeDisplaySelector">
        <property name="enabled">
         <bool>false</bool>
        </property>
        <property name="toolTip">
         <string>Bands: the calibrated cube one band at a time, with the band's wavelength on the panel; scroll the panel to change band. Colour preview: the bands nearest 650, 550 and 470 nm shown as red, green and blue, reflectance 0 to 1.0 on one fixed scale. It is a band composite, not a photograph. Click a pixel of HS Cube in either view to plot its spectrum under Pixel spectrum.</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
     </layout>
    </widget>
